In this course you will explore the history and significance of democracy. In particular, you will explore:

- The origins of democratic thought in ancient Greece;
- The development of democratic institutions in the late medieval and early modern period;
- The rise of the nation state as a form of political organization and its relation to democracy;
- The role of liberalism and capitalism in the development of modern democracies;
- The growth of mass politics and the relationship between democracy and economic equality;
- The question of whether there can be such a thing as “global” democracy; and
- The future of democracy in the wake of globalization.

